{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[E]For many years I've been a rolling stone my [A]darling
Like a [E]gypsy I have roamed from place to [B7]place
Fortune [E]never came to me how [A]happy I would be
Just to [E]look again upon [B7]your smiling [E]face
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Now if I should [E]wander back tonight would you be [A]waiting
Would your [E]eyes be filled with love's own tender [B7]light
Would your [E]arms be empty [E7]dear would you [A]thrill to find me [A7]near
Would you [E]love me if I'd [B7]wander back [E]tonight
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
When budding flowers lend their fragrance in the springtime
I recall the roses twining round your door
Fancy then I homeward stay and I seem to hear you say
That you love me as you did in days of yore
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Last night I dreamed that you and I were back together
I held your hand so gently in my own
Heard you say we'd never part as I pressed you to my heart
Then I woke in tears to find myself alone
{end_of_chorus}
